WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.960
He may have dazzled audiences as&nbsp;
sparkly vampire Edward Cullen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.140
but behind the scenes, Robert&nbsp;
Pattinson had a dirty little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.100
secret. Here's the gross habit that could&nbsp;
make fans see him in a whole new light.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.060
The "Twilight" saga has everything you&nbsp;
could possibly want in a teen romance:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:21.540
star-crossed lovers, a shockingly good soundtrack,&nbsp;
and a creepy telepathic baby. And instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.940
sleeping in dusty old coffins, these vampires are&nbsp;
glimmering immortals, beautiful beyond compare.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:32.520
However, Bella Swan still has a hard time choosing&nbsp;
between the mysterious Edward Cullen and the moody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.320
werewolf Jacob Black. It seems like it would&nbsp;
be a pretty easy decision, especially because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.480
Edward and the other vampires constantly remark&nbsp;
that Jacob and the werewolves carry a foul stench&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.860
with them wherever they go. But apparently,&nbsp;
the situation is reversed in real life.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.200
During a 2012 interview with Extra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.220
Pattinson was asked to address a comment&nbsp;
he made about not washing his hair for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.720
six weeks, and his answer would send every&nbsp;
scent-sensitive vampire running for the hills.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.120
"I don't really see the&nbsp;
point in washing your hair."&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.380
"To be clean, maybe?"&nbsp;

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.920
"If you don't care if your hair's clean&nbsp;
or not then why would you wash it?"

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.180
Pattinson then compared his unwashed&nbsp;
hair to his untidy living space, saying,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.980
"It's like, I don't clean my apartment 'cause I&nbsp;
don't care. I have my apartment for sleeping in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.960
and I have my hair for just, you know, hanging out&nbsp;
on my head. I don't care if it's clean or not."

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.920
It can be hard to be objective about your&nbsp;
own cleanliness, but it's impossible to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.600
know the truth when other sources have made&nbsp;
conflicting comments about Pattinson's hygiene.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.280
The vampires in "Twilight" don't sweat, so&nbsp;
readers might like to imagine that Edward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.060
smells like the pages of the books&nbsp;
in his bedroom and the crisp forest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.740
air after climbing all those trees with Bella.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, one source says that Pattinson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.960
smelled badly enough on set that it affected&nbsp;
his coworkers. An anonymous crew member who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.740
worked closely with Pattinson during the&nbsp;
production of "New Moon" told E! News,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.520
"He stinks. I mean, it's awful. He never showers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.420
and it drives people on the set&nbsp;
crazy. [...] He completely reeks."

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.620
Knowing that Pattinson himself said that he&nbsp;
doesn't have the best hygiene habits sucks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:05.220
the romance out of all those scenes where&nbsp;
Edward and Bella get up in each other's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.720
personal space. However, his co-star has&nbsp;
her own opinion on the subject. Kristen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.860
Stewart told People before the first&nbsp;
film hit theaters in November 2008,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.800
"He smells great. It's kind of an animalist thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.740
that goes on. It went along with&nbsp;
the movie, so it was perfect."

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.700
Pattinson has notoriously mocked the&nbsp;
"Twilight" franchise over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.900
so he clearly has a sense of humor. His&nbsp;
comments about hygiene could be true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.400
or just another self-deprecating joke.&nbsp;
Either way, Pattinson apparently made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.420
some improvements to his self-care routine&nbsp;
after the "Twilight" franchise wrapped.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.040
In 2013, it was announced that the actor&nbsp;
would become the face of Dior Homme fragrance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.500
which the company describes as having an alluring,&nbsp;
earthy scent. Surely a luxury brand like the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:51.240
of Dior wouldn't tap Pattinson for the job if&nbsp;
they didn't think his image could sell cologne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.660
though the actor admits that partnering&nbsp;
with the company may have, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.400
improved his skincare regimen. Pattinson&nbsp;
explained to the Wall Street Journal in 2014,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.920
"I was a brush-your-teeth-and-have-a-shower kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.120
of guy. I can't tell if it's because of my&nbsp;
association with Dior or because I'm older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.840
but I've started moisturizing. It's been&nbsp;
a quite profound change in my life."

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.340
"I like my smell."

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.260
An anonymous source from a movie set more than&nbsp;
a decade ago hardly counts as evidence. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.100
Pattinson’s apparent disregard for&nbsp;
hygiene may surprise some. As the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.740
"Twilight" saga gears up to return as a TV series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.840
fans may wonder whether they prefer the new&nbsp;
Edward or the allegedly foul-smelling original.

